# group_bind.tkr — the §9.D Reseed-1 ACCEPT host for capability (c): the anonymous group-bind pattern
# `(B | C) as v`, which matches AND binds a NESTED anonymous union member of a union-of-unions subject
# `A | (B | C)` (kept nested, never flattened — §9.D). Each scenario names itself and asserts its
# announced value through `run` in `main.tks`, so a relapse names itself. Inert on the seed: the corpus
# writes no group-bind pattern — this is an additive capability.

Feature: group_bind — §9.D anonymous group-bind pattern `(B | C) as v` (Reseed 1, capability c)

  Scenario: group_arm — the group arm fires on the nested member, distinct from the direct `A` arm (A=1, group=2 → 12)
    When built and run
    Then stdout pattern = "scenario group_arm: ok"

  Scenario: rebind_inner — `(B | C) as v` binds the whole nested variant; re-matching `v` reads the leaf payload (C.c=30 → 230)
    When built and run
    Then stdout pattern = "scenario rebind_inner: ok"

  Scenario: group_exhaustive — `A` + `(B | C) as v` is exhaustive with no `_`; both arms run (A.a=1 + B.b nested=120 → 121)
    When built and run
    Then stdout pattern = "scenario group_exhaustive: ok"

  Scenario: group_opt — `(B | C) as v` over an OPTIONAL `(B | C) | null` field binds the present union and re-matches its leaf (B.b=40 → 340)
    When built and run
    Then stdout pattern = "scenario group_opt: ok"
